    {
      "id": "D4",
      "name": "the same anchor is worth a third as much wrapped in commentary",
      "traces": [
        "F1",
        "D4-prime"
      ],
      "notes": "Both articles cite the same model at 20%. The first reports it and nothing else (weight 4.0); the second surrounds it with three paragraphs of comment, dropping to (4.0 + 3×0.25)/4 = 1.1875 — and the commentary does not merely dilute the anchor's weight, it erases its direction: the article's stance is exactly 0.0, the -0.6 anchor cancelled claim-for-claim by opinion. Identical evidence, opposite contribution, decided entirely by how much colour the outlet wrapped around it — the mixed-class credibility drop the D4' trace named. (evidence_weight is rounded to 3dp on the response.)",
